{"format":1,"version":0,"generated_at":"2026-09-26T20:33:24.163Z","exam":{"slug":"jamb","name":"JAMB"},"subject":{"slug":"physics","name":"Physics","display_name":"Physics"},"topics":[],"papers":[{"id":-1,"year":2025,"title":"Physics sample questions","duration_minutes":null,"items":[{"id":-22,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the SI unit of force?</p>","options":{"A":"joule","B":"newton","C":"watt","D":"pascal"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Force is measured in newtons (N).</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>We dey measure force for newtons (N).</p>"},{"id":-23,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Speed is calculated as</p>","options":{"A":"distance × time","B":"distance ÷ time","C":"time ÷ distance","D":"mass ÷ time"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Speed = distance ÷ time.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Speed = distance divide time.</p>"},{"id":-24,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the SI unit of energy?</p>","options":{"A":"joule","B":"newton","C":"hertz","D":"ampere"},"answer":"A","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Energy is measured in joules (J).</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>We dey measure energy for joules (J).</p>"},{"id":-25,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Which of these is a vector quantity?</p>","options":{"A":"mass","B":"time","C":"velocity","D":"temperature"},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Velocity has both size and direction.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Velocity get size and direction.</p>"},{"id":-26,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Light travels fastest in</p>","options":{"A":"water","B":"glass","C":"air","D":"a vacuum"},"answer":"D","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Light is fastest in a vacuum.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Light dey fastest for vacuum.</p>"},{"id":-27,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>At normal pressure, water boils at</p>","options":{"A":"50 °C","B":"75 °C","C":"100 °C","D":"150 °C"},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Water boils at 100 °C.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Water dey boil at 100 °C.</p>"},{"id":-28,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Which instrument measures electric current?</p>","options":{"A":"voltmeter","B":"ammeter","C":"barometer","D":"thermometer"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>An ammeter measures current.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Ammeter dey measure current.</p>"},{"id":-29,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the unit of frequency?</p>","options":{"A":"hertz","B":"metre","C":"kilogram","D":"volt"},"answer":"A","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Frequency is measured in hertz (Hz).</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>We dey measure frequency for hertz (Hz).</p>"}]}]}